A cozy Singapore HDB apartment interior in the style of Vincent van Gogh, featuring swirling brushstrokes of warm yellows and deep blues. In the center, an imaginative children's loft bed with built-in storage compartments and a hidden play cave underneath, rendered with thick impasto texture and expressive curved lines. Scattered across a wooden table in the foreground are rolled architectural sketches and small wooden model pieces. Through a window, the distinctive silhouette of Singapore public housing blocks appears against a starry, turbulent night sky. The room glows with domestic warmth, toys peeking from cubbies, pillows arranged on the creative bed structure, capturing the excitement of new beginnings and the joy of designing spaces for children to dream and play.
